# Specification - Taskwarrior WebUI Enhancement

## Requirements
Reimplement and incorporate all features from Taskwarrior Web (webui1 - https://github.com/tmahmood/taskwarrior-web) into taskwarrior-webui (webui2 - https://github.com/DCsunset/taskwarrior-webui), on the target fork https://github.com/pplupo/taskwarrior-webui. Also create a TWKB-inspired (https://github.com/DerTimonius/twkb) Kanban view.

Core Features:
1. Keyboard Navigation & Mnemonic Overlay Engine: Ctrl+Shift+K focus, 1-2 character mnemonic red-box badges on tasks, tags, projects, and custom queries.
2. Active Task & Timer (Timewarrior) Integration: Active Task bar widget (+ACTIVE status), toggle timer (start/stop), auto-stopping running tasks when starting a new one.
3. Undo System & Revert Preview: Operations revert report (/tasks/undo/report) preview before executing task undo.
4. Custom Queries Engine: Configurable custom Taskwarrior queries via TOML/env vars with fixed shortcut keys or auto mnemonics.
5. Task Details & Direct CLI Modifiers: Dependency tree view sorted by completion status, annotation manager, and free-form Taskwarrior command modification input.
6. TWKB-inspired Kanban Board View:
   - Columns: To Do, In Progress, Waiting, Done.
   - Cards with project/tag chips, urgency, priority badges, blocked/recurring indicators, due date warnings.
   - Drag-and-drop state transitions (drag to In Progress starts timer, drag to Done completes task).
   - Card inline quick actions (start/stop, done, edit, block, delete).
7. Gantt Chart View:
   - Timeline display with deterministic horizontal date sequencing:
     - Primary: Use `task.start`.
     - Secondary: If no start date, fallback to `task.due`.
     - Tertiary: If neither, place after completion of latest prerequisite task (`task.depends`).
     - Quaternary: If no dates and no prerequisites exist, place at today (`00:00:00`).
     - Duration / Length: When both start and due dates exist, span all calendar columns from start date through due date inclusive (advancing to start of following day); otherwise default to 1 day.
   - Calendarless "Sequence" View Mode:
     - "Sequence" view option in zoom controls: renders the exact visual card layout and spacing as the daily view, completely decoupled from calendar dates.
     - Sequential step columns ("Step 1", "Step 2", "Step 3"...) with no calendar dates or day subtitles.
     - Starts strictly at the column/day of the very first task (`Step 1`), eliminating the 3-day past buffer used by the Day view.
   - Deterministic 4-tier vertical sorting:
     - Tier 1: Priority (`H` > `M` > `L` > no priority set placed last).
     - Tier 2: Taskwarrior urgency (descending order).
     - Tier 3: Dependents count (descending count of downstream tasks listing this task in `depends`).
     - Tier 4: Alphabetical order by description (`localeCompare`).
   - "Filter as you type" search:
     - Text input in Gantt control header with real-time partial case-insensitive filtering on description.
     - Two-way synchronized with URL query parameter (`?search=...`) with debounced route persistence.
   - Fluid timeline zoom & horizontal scroll preservation:
     - Interactive zoom options (`Sequence`, `Day`, `Week`, `Month`) with two-way URL persistence (`?zoom=...`).
     - Elimination of empty weeks and empty months: Week view strictly spans from Monday of the earliest task to Sunday of the latest task; Month view strictly spans from the 1st of the earliest task's month to the last day of the latest task's month without artificial padding.
     - Uncompressed layout with smooth horizontal scrolling (`overflow-x: auto`): enforces generous minimum column widths (`140px` for Sequence/Day, `700px` for Week guaranteeing ~100px/day, `1500px` for Month guaranteeing ~50px/day) while expanding dynamically (`Math.max(minColWidth, distributed)`) to fill wide viewports, eliminating empty void space when sparse while preventing crowded column compression when populated.
     - Status filters (`Active & Pending`, `Completed`, `All (Excl. Deleted)`).
   - End-to-Start Dependency Visualization:
     - Non-overlapping multi-track orthogonal SVG connector routing across all zoom modes (Sequence, Day, Week, Month), guaranteeing that vertical lines have dedicated tracks, never cross through any intermediate task card/component, never overlap, never continue past arrowheads, and never produce >2 line crossings at any intersection.
     - Semicircular bridge hops (`A 4 4 0 0 0`) for crossing lines.
   - Interactive Anchor Dependency Management:
     - Left (destination) and right (source) anchor handles on task bars.
     - Click/drag from a right anchor highlights target left anchors and creates a Taskwarrior dependency on release/click.
     - Bidirectional linking support: dragging from left anchor points arrow into left anchor.
     - Hovering over a dependency SVG arrow reveals a stable, debounced "X" delete button to remove the dependency relationship.
   - Seamless view switcher between "Tasks" (Table/List), "Kanban" (Board), and "Gantt" (Timeline).
8. Reporting Module: Project progress tracking rings and burndown charts.
9. Enhanced Usability: Tag text copy button, customizable columns/colors, and theme toggling (Light/Dark/Auto).

## User Stories
As a Taskwarrior user, I want a modern web interface that combines full keyboard shortcuts, active task timer tracking, undo previews, and custom query reports from webui1 with a responsive Vuetify UI.
As a Taskwarrior user, I want a Kanban board view inspired by twkb so I can visually organize, drag-and-drop, and track tasks across To Do, In Progress, Waiting, and Done columns.
As a Taskwarrior user, I want a Gantt chart view option alongside Tasks and Kanban views so I can visually analyze task timelines, dependencies, and schedules.
As a developer, I want all these features cleanly integrated into the Koa backend and Vue.js frontend of pplupo/taskwarrior-webui.
